RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
February 22, 2016
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Jim Brown, Bryan Cook, Richard Johnson, Mike Luna, Dr. Mark Rinne, Scott Roybal,
Dicky Shanor, Annette Williams and Jeff White.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, and Dan
White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda.  (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion. There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Cook moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded by
Mr. Luna.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on February 8, 2016.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Luna moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Ms. Williams.
Upon inquiry, Mayor Kaysen, Lois Huff, City Treasurer, and Brandon Cammarata, Development
Director, provided information available on vouchers payable to the following: Altitude Recycling
Equipment, LLC (baling wire for compressing recyclable materials); Art Payroll (contract labor to
assist with Civic Center productions); Ayers Associates, Inc. (contract for environmental services
for the West Edge project); Aztec Construction Company, Inc. (demolition of existing billboards on
Swan Ranch Industrial Park); Chick-Fil-A and Sam’s Club (food purchases for concession stand at
Ice & Events Center).  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
Mayor Kaysen opened a public hearing to receive comments and input for renewal
applications for existing City liquor licenses (retail, restaurant, limited retail, resort, bar and grill
licenses, and microbrewery permits) filed with the City Clerk’s Office.  Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk,
noted that included with the renewal applications are six licenses in “parked” status, and that six
current licensees did not file for renewal for the upcoming year.  Mayor Kaysen advised Chief Brian
Kozak, Police Department, was unable to be present at the meeting to review the department’s report
on compliance checks conducted throughout 2015 and that Chief Kozak would provide a report at
the March 7th Finance Committee meeting.  He further advised that Chief Kozak had indicated there
were no department issues that would affect license renewals.  There being no further comments and
purpose of the public hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the hearing and referred the
applications to Finance Committee.
ORDINANCE - 3rd READING - Amending Section 2.40.035(B), Traffic School-
Administrative Fee, of Chapter 2.40, Municipal Court, of Title 2, Administration and Personnel, of
```

### Page 2 of 5

```text
the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming.  Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr. Brown moved
to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Mark Moran, Senior Municipal Court
Judge, advised the purpose of amending the fee is to recover program costs, noting the current fee
of $25.00 has not been increased for 10 years.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the
governing body with the exception of Mr. Cook and Dr. Rinne voting “no”. (#4120)
ORDINANCE - 2 READING - Amending Section 10.32.030, Decreasing State Speed
nd
Limits in Certain Zones, of Chapter 10.32, Speed Limits, of Title 10, Vehicle and Traffic, of the
Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming.  Bart Stolp questioned whether the proposed amendment
would affect Van Buren Avenue and Pinto Lane.  Mayor Kaysen advised a traffic analysis will be
conducted generally throughout the City.  Reporting for Public Services Committee, Dr. Rinne
moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  It was noted the ordinance, if
approved, will amend the current 25 mph speed limit in residential zones to 30 mph to be in
compliance with state statutes which requires a speed study before the limit could be changed.  Upon
inquiry, Mayor Kaysen clarified when City Code was changed in 2004 to implement the 25 mph
speed limit the City did not conduct the necessary speed study as required and advised this ordinance
will place the City in compliance until the necessary studies can be done.  Discussion topics included
the following: 2004 ordinance change; necessary traffic study per state law; current speed limit
signage at entry points into the City; what constitutes a legal speed study; enforcement; streets that
will be involved in the speed study (collector, arterial and Central Business District); speed studies
that have been conducted for portions of Pershing Blvd., Van Buren and Pinto Lane, and compliance
with state statute.  John Hall, City Engineer, provided information on the upcoming speed control
study that will involve certain streets; study requirements per state statute and state rules; changing
of current entry signage into the City from 25 to 30 mph; anticipated time frame (approximately six
months) in which to conduct the speed study; difference between design speeds as referenced in the
Unified Development Code vs. speed limits, and statutory speed limits for school zones.  Upon
inquiry, Dan White, City Attorney, provided information on the 30 mph speed limit established by
state statute and speed limit enforcement generally.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members
of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Williams voting “no”.
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Certifying that the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne concurs with
the application of the Board of County Commissioners of Laramie County, Wyoming, for an award
of Fiscal Year 2013-2014 Countywide Consensus Block Grant Funding in the amount of $2,201.37
for the Stone Trash Receptacles Project for the Town of Pine Bluffs.  Motion (per Consent Agenda)
carried. (#5751)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Certifying that the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne concurs with
the application of the Board of County Commissioners of Laramie County, Wyoming, for an award
of Fiscal Year 2015-2016 Countywide Consensus Block Grant Funding in the amount of $107,618
for a replacement loader for the Town of Pine Bluffs.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
(#5752)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Re-appropriating the Fiscal Year 2016 budget of the City of Cheyenne
according to the provisions of W.S. §16-4-112 and 16-4-113.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
(#5753)
