### Page 5 of 5

```text
5719 Yellowstone Road, Cheyenne, Wyoming.
Announcement was made of the Re-Appointment of William C. Beaman to the City of
Cheyenne, Wyoming - Laramie County, State of Wyoming Joint Powers Board for Frontier Park
Improvements, to be confirmed March 14, 2016.
Under other business:
Bart Stolp, referenced  a January 16, 2016 newspaper article and commented on neighbors’
traffic and pedestrian safety concerns, noting his observations involving safety issues on Van Buren
Avenue near a school crosswalk.  Upon inquiry, John Hall, City Engineer, provided information on
improvements and installation costs, and noted more sidewalk work is planned after the current
school year.  Mr. Stolp expressed his disagreement with results of a speed study conducted by the
City in the vicinity and stated drivers’ compliance with the speed limit is evident only when there
is a visible police presence.
Jeff Dierksen commented on recent adoption of the revised Neighborhood Traffic
Management Program (NTMP) and his concerns with elimination of the Neighborhood Traffic
Committee and speed watch portion of the program and changes in eligibility criteria and the point
system.  He proposed presentations be provided by the Metropolitan Planning Organization to
members of the governing body to explain the program and program aspects that have been changed.
Upon inquiry to Mayor Kaysen regarding answers to past questions posed by Mr. Dierksen, Mayor
Kaysen reported he was still working on response information.
Ms. Williams referenced action taken at the February 8, 2016 City Council meeting regarding
adoption of a resolution for the Traffic Signal Project on Walterscheid and Fox Farm and 5 St. and
th
Deming Drive.  It was noted the resolution authorized submittal of a Mineral Royalty Capital
Construction Account grant funding application to the State Loan and Investment Board for the
project and that SLIB has not yet met to review the application.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 7:15 p.m.

Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
March 3, 2016
